Summing the areas:
A = \frac{11}{6} + \frac{10}{3} = \frac{11+20}{6} = \frac{31}{6}
The problem asks for \(12A\).
12A = 12\left(\frac{31}{6}\right) = 2 \times 31 = 62
The value of 12A is 62.

